Z||000014||HarryG||07-20-2001||12:30 PM||||What Scott mentioned is also called "tuft testing" and can be done by using 6"-8" pieces of yarn taped to the body where you want to observe the air flow. You arrange the yarn pieces in a row across the body panel and orient them so they're 90 degrees to the airflow. The tape goes across the middle of each piece.  Use a contrasting color of yarn so it will be plainly visible in the photos or videos which your friends can take as they drive alongside (or since you're interested in the wing, they can shoot pix through the back glass?) ||||reg||1
