Z||000016||Toddster||07-20-2001||12:51 PM||||A lot of people seem to forget that the Fiero had one of the largest wings of any production car ever!<P>They also seem to forget that the Plymouth SuperBird was claimed to have an "unfair" advantage in the 70-71 Trans Am series due to its innovative wing.<P>Sure, there are a variety of wings out there that are purely cosmetic (the Gen 3 Firebird comes to mind) some people assume that they are all just about looks. Speaking exclusively as a person who deems highway speed limits as "self governing and optional" I for one can attest to the difference in handling of a winged car versus a non-winged car at speed.||||reg||1
