Z||000018||Formula||07-20-2001||01:13 PM||||heres my only test on the wing so far...<P>wash the car down, drive down the road and come back, the front will dry first along with the hood and the roof, the sides will dry off for the most part, and last the decklid and wing will dry off.  it takes a lot longer for the wing to dry off, look at it while your driving, the water doesnt even move... is this functional or not?||||reg||1
Z||000019||rogergarrison||07-20-2001||01:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Toddster:<BR><B><BR>They also seem to forget that the Plymouth SuperBird was claimed to have an "unfair" advantage in the 70-71 Trans Am series due to its innovative wing.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>ya but were talkin a race car thats capable of 200+ mph, and that wing was adjustable too. I think were talkin 70 mph speeds here. I think everyone conceeds that over 150 mph or so almost any wing/spoiler is going to have some effect, whether its good or bad. Driving to work on the interstate, that wing isnt going to give ya any kind of usable downforce. Its looks - case closed.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000020||The Fieromaster||07-20-2001||02:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierosound:<BR><B><BR>The rear wing produces up to 250 lbs of rear downforce (varies with speed).  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thats BS really big stinky BS... Look at your luggage rack info in your manual!! The deck lid can only suppor under 200 pounds or so...  AND go out spray your spoiler with water and get your ass on the freeway.. look the water stays there... that means no wind is hitting it.. Someone is BS someone... not saying its you though.. I love my spoiler!<P>------------------<BR>      <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT><BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">        <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT></B>||||reg||1
