Z||000037||California Kid||07-21-2001||07:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by filthyscarecrow:<BR><B>dude, cali kid, the mistake yuo made is that you assumed that you can do the testing without reading the book first. how will you know what you're looking at if you don't know how it's supposed to work. you never mentioned anything about principles of fluid dynamics in your argument, do you understnad them? if not, how do you expect to understand what the wing is doing when you tape your little pieces of yarn to it. the reason books and papers exist is so that we can use a general guideline to determine WHETHER to test in the first place. if you read the books, you'll understand that there's no point in testing the wing because based on principles we already know, the wing is a decoration. why waste the time and money testing to find out something we can figure out using common sense and a couple books? eh, i guess it's your time and money... let me know how it turns out.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Dude, I don't assume anything !!! If everyone applied the same logic that you have above, we'd still be riding carriages pulled by horses for transportation.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000038||Cozmo||07-21-2001||09:12 AM||||There's a pic in Gary Witzenburg's "Fiero" book of an IMSA bodied Fiero in a wind tunnel.  I let someone borrow my copy, but I think the pic showed smoke being blown over the car at a pretty high rate.  If someone has this, maybe they could post the pic and it would give us some more info to discuss.<P>As far as the real world "tuft" testing, our club is going to do it and film it with a variety of configurations.  It may not be "emperical data", but it's really just an excuse for us Fieroites to get together and talk about our cars anyway <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Imagine what bystanders will think when they see a pack of Fieros go by with one of them covered with brightly colored pieces of yarn...<P><BR><B>C02M0</B> ||||reg||1
