Z||000040||rogergarrison||07-21-2001||07:57 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by California Kid:<BR><B>Reply to rogergarrison: I'm just thankful you're not designing aircraft.<P>Last Post I promise !!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR> <BR>I gave up trying to explain logic. I had to post to reply since yours is directed to me.<BR>I do design and fly my own now.10 years ago me and a friend in Pt Clinton, Ohio, designed and built a 4 place single engine experimental plane, mostly of fiberglass. I almost forgot about that. And last time I talked to him it still is flying quite well. Im sure he'll have it at Oshgosh this week if you want to check it out. I also design and fly radio control models. but aerodynamic priciples are equal model or real. and yes they all worked quite well. Give it up dude   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> trade your Fiero in on a Honda and apply all your aerodynamics like the ricer boys. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 07-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000041||rogergarrison||07-21-2001||08:27 PM||||I just got back from Vintage Gran Prix and heres a sorta related question for you. I passed a Neon, all the usual, huge wing (sigh), white tail lights, decals all over. the interesting thing is it had ground effects, looked homemade. in the front, rear and down both rocker panels. the wierd part is they stuck straight out all the way around like running boards. Now, id be interested in your theory on any possible use they would have like that..........<P>my theory is they water ski/hydroplane nicely thru deep water. I quess this would be under hydrodynamics.||||reg||13
Z||000042||Ken Wittlief||07-22-2001||02:18 AM||||those arnt ground effects - those are running boards!<P>  ground effects are most beneficial when they almost scrape the ground - not too cool pulling out of the driveway though, or at the parking lots with the yellow railroad ties between spaces.||||reg||11
Z||000043||Galen||07-22-2001||04:16 AM||||"THe optional rear deck spoiler, along with the aerodynamic package, not only help give the car the look of a performance machine, but reduce the Fiero's already impressive .377 drag coefficient to a drago coefficent of .350"<P>That is quoted from the 85 Do It Yourself service manual.Anyone wanna argue with GM?<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple">"It may be the opinion of the court, but its still wrong"</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/download.html" TARGET=_blank>Download FieroProject.com Chat Client v1.22 Today</A>||||reg||1
